This repository presents an end-to-end time series forecasting framework for predicting Carbon Monoxide (CO) and Nitrogen Dioxide (NO₂) concentrations using two widely adopted forecasting approaches:
- Prophet
- Vector AutoRegression (VAR)
The project covers data preprocessing, exploratory data analysis (EDA), feature engineering, model development, forecasting, evaluation, and visualization.

Features
- Time Series Forecasting
- Data Cleaning
- Missing Value Handling
- Date-Time Feature Engineering
- Prophet Forecasting
- VAR Forecasting
- Performance Evaluation
- Visualization
- Modular Code
- Reproducible Results



Technologies
- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Prophet
- Statsmodels
- Scikit-learn


Evaluation Metrics
- Mean Absolute Error (MAE)
- Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)
- Mean Absolute Percentage Error (MAPE)
- R² Score



Output
- Forecast plots
- Residual plots
- Prediction CSV
- Evaluation report




